  "narrative": "I use the controller signed convention: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency in the claimed direction; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means weaker dependency in the claimed direction. The corrected registration refines the accepted dataset-specific core without relying on invalid parent links. Batch_a is the largest screen batch and has not yet been used as a direct stratification check. I therefore test the accepted SMARCA4 and PTEN stronger-dependency contrasts and the accepted TP53 and KEAP1 weaker-dependency contrasts within batch_a. Persistence of all four would make screen-batch composition a less plausible explanation for the accepted associations; attenuation would indicate residual technical or batch-context dependence. I also test PTEN at stricter screen quality, screen_roc_auc >= 0.96, because PTEN is accepted but its precise magnitude relative to the 0.15-unit threshold is less tightly localized than SMARCA4, TP53, or KEAP1. A lower bound above 0.15 would strengthen PTEN as a robust main dataset marker; a wide or null interval would keep PTEN supported but context-sensitive. I register SMARCA4 among lines lacking DNA omics as a technical-availability robustness check for the strongest accepted association. High hypoxia is tested for TP53 and KEAP1 as a stress-state context; high hypoxia might preserve, dilute, or modify the accepted weaker-dependency associations. PTEN is also tested within ARID1A-loss lines to ask whether PTEN's moderate stronger-dependency signal persists on a related SWI/SNF co-loss background. For broader molecular exploration, APC is tested in high WNT activity and MYC amplification is tested in high MYC expression to ask whether otherwise weak markers show concordant context-specific effects. Finally, a constructed research_signature_c interaction is tested against SMARCA4 because this assay has no assigned biological role and therefore provides a conservative falsification test for an unassigned constructed modifier. All proposed comparisons are associations in the supplied dataset; they do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round 7 explore notes. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger/more negative dependency; direction +1 positive = weaker/less negative dependency. Current dataset-supported core: SMARCA4 loss strongest robust stronger-dependency marker; TP53 and KEAP1 loss robust weaker-dependency markers; PTEN moderate stronger-dependency marker with strict co-intact validation; CDKN2A modest stronger-dependency only in clean strict TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 contexts. New exploration priorities: batch_a stratification for SMARCA4, PTEN, TP53, KEAP1; stricter PTEN screen_roc_auc >=0.96; SMARCA4 in DNA-omics-missing lines; TP53 and KEAP1 under strict quality in high hypoxia; PTEN within ARID1A-loss; APC in high WNT activity; MYC amplification in high MYC expression; SMARCA4 interaction with high research_signature_c. Existing queued unresolved claims include H102-H107 maximal clean-intact refinements and several context checks. Interpret all findings as dataset-specific associations and keep biological interpretation uncertain."
